  "query_preview": "..\n\nRest of Today through Monday...\n\nPatchy fog may develop tonight through Wednesday morning, with\nlighter winds across southern Montana and northern Wyoming. The \nbest chance for fog development exists around and east of \nBillings. Use caution during the Wednesday morning commute as \nreductions to visibility could impact travel.\n\nWeak ridging will build over the Northern Rockies through midweek.\nTemperatures will be in the 40s to 50sF today and Wednesday,  \nbefore increasing further into the 50s and low 60sF Thursday and\nFriday. The chance for precipitation is very low (less than 10%)\nacross the lower elevations through the weekend. Ensembles do show\na shortwave trough moving across the area on Friday. This wave \ndoes not look to bring much precipitation aside from isolated \nshowers in the mountains.\n\nThe most impactful weather in the forecast period will be Friday \nand through Sunday, when models are depicting an increasing \npressure gradient developing over the Paradise Valley. While the \ngradient orientation is not the perfect setup for gap winds in the\nLivingston and Nye areas, there is currently a moderate chance \n(40 to 60%)for wind gusts of 50 mph or higher Friday and Saturday \nnight. Breezy conditions may also impact the US-191 corridor from\nBig Timber through Harlowton, with winds gusting in the range of\n25 to 40 mph.\n\nMatos",
